            <ArticleTitle>Microbial transformation of resveratrol by endophyte Streptomyces sp. A12 isolated from Polygonum cuspidatum.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>1-4</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.1080/14786419.2017.1405411</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Resveratrol (1) undergoes microbial transformation when fermented with Streptomyces sp. A12 to yield 3, 5, 4'-trimethoxy-trans-stilbene (2). The structure of the compound 2 was elucidated using the modern spectroscopic techniques. This is the first report of the microbial transformation of resveratrol to compound 2 using the endophyte isolated from Polygonum cuspidatum.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
